  "category": "highway",
  "name": {
    "en": "A2 Hemus Motorway"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "The Hemus Motorway (A2) is Bulgaria's primary north-south highway connecting Sofia to the Black Sea port city of Varna via Shumen. The 418 km motorway crosses the Balkan Mountains and duplicates three European routes (E70, E83, E772). As of December 2025, 206 km are operational in two disconnected segments: Sofia to Ugarchin (approximately 103 km) and Buhovtsi to Varna (approximately 108 km). A substantial gap of approximately 208 km remains between Ugarchin and Buhovtsi under construction or in planning phases. Construction officially began on October 4, 1974, with the first section opening in 1999. The motorway is managed by the Bulgarian Roads Agency (successor to NCSIP)."
  },
